WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.980
Sorry for making you come with me to a place like this.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:07.720
Not at all!

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.110
Helping out with research is part of R&D's responsibilities.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.640
Thank you.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.320
Not much is known about this ruin,

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:19.160
so it would have been dangerous for me to come alone.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:20.290
Huh?

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.650
This tablet...

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.270
Didn't we find something similar before?

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.520
That's right.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.520
I'll take it and look into it later.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.300
Oh?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.640
Did you guys find some treasure?

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.140
Reyfer-san!

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.640
What are you doing here?

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.270
That's a mean way to greet me.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.730
I actually have permission to exterminate monsters here today.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.770
My senses as a treasure hunter are especially useful...

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.720
...in ruins like this one that haven't been thoroughly explored.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.950
Really?

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.540
Of course!

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.000
The most important thing during a dungeon expedition is the ability to find all the hidden rooms and pathways.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.900
That's where you can usually find hidden treasure.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.250
It's also important not to touch any hidden traps.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.300
I heard the wall move just now!

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.960
K-Keep calm!

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:19.760
Based on my experience, these kinds of mechanisms usually cause a hidden room to appear-

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.260
The wall!

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.020
Could it be a hidden room?

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.520
Something loud is heading this way!

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.940
Everyone, run!

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.990
You imbecile!

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:25.970
What'd ya think?

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.520
Thrilling, wasn't it?

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.060
I don't need that kind of thrill.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.690
But look at that entrance over there.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.320
This room...

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.950
What an amazing mural.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.060
This is my first time seeing one.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.950
This is my first time seeing such a large mural.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:51.580
Huh?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.540
What's this?

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:56.590
It's a notebook.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.740
But that's a modern artifact, isn't it?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.970
There's a name on it.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.840
Keithgrif

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.630
Uncle Keith?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.560
Excuse us!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.270
Come in.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.480
It's messier than the last time we were here.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.360
Since you're here, how about cleaning up the office for me?

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:23.880
Threia-san, don't tell me that's why you asked us to come over.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.270
I was kidding.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.950
I was thinking of reporting what we found in our ruins investigation.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.960
We picked up a notebook left behind by my uncle, Keithgrif.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.430
Your uncle?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.520
That's right.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.590
My uncle was both an alchemist and a researcher.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.260
He explored and investigated ruins everywhere and he even ruined a few.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:45.800
Ruined?

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.950
That's just who he is.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.520
Of course, Central City is searching for him now.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:56.480
I think I heard of a similar story before.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:01.750
He kept his notes about the ruins in this book.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.360
Reading it helped me understand a lot.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:13.870
We can think of the wall painting as an important message about why the people of the previous era were eradicated.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:18.750
It's true that it seemed to be a civilisation with very advanced alchemical technology.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.490
Several theories exist for why they were destroyed.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:25.880
The cause may have been depletion of resources, war, or even self-destruction.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:32.270
This picture shows there were many countries working together to create the ruins.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:38.440
In those ruins, people researched the growing of plants on barren land.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:42.020
Everyone worked together to fill the world with plants!

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.650
That's wonderful!

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.700
But in the end, the people from the last era were destroyed.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:53.950
Despite working together with such advanced technology, they weren't able survive in the end.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.580
I wonder if my uncle is trying to tell me something.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.470
What path did the humans of the past take?

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.420
And in what direction will they travel in the future?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.060
I need more information.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.680
There are still ruins like that last one that no one has reached yet.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:10.930
The Unexplored Ruins!

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.470
That's right.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.680
Nobody has ever made it there.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.510
There are bound to be new discoveries there!

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.790
It's my dream to reach that place!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.210
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:28.530
Also, I'm looking for the other pieces of this tablet.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.790
That kind of looks like the Unexplored Ruins.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.780
Yeah, I had that same thought.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.350
There's a girl above the Unexplored Ruins.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.750
I wonder if it means anything.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:43.050
We might just find out if we can reach those ruins.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:50.730
I'm submitting an official request to R&D to survey the Unexplored Ruins.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.350
Please hand it to Marion.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.840
Yes!

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.810
Thank you!

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:01.110
Oh, Marion-san, I have a request from Threia-san.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.910
Escha-chan, Logy-kun,

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.400
we're having an emergency meeting.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.360
Everyone is here, I see.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.380
I know this is sudden, but Central City just contacted us.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:21.370
Next season, Central City will send a team for surveying the Unexplored Ruins to Colseit.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:23.630
Central?

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:27.090
Branch Manager, what about us?

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.890
Will the Colseit Branch join the survey team?

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:34.890
I did not receive any instructions about participating in the survey.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:39.100
Our job is to protect the ruins before the survey team arrives,

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.160
and to find a way to reach the ruins.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.060
That is all.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.820
Doesn't that mean we're just paving the way for them?!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.950
I will issue further instructions later.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.590
That concludes our meeting.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.250
You are dismissed for the day.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.650
No way. No way!

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.210
Marion...

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.050
Are they telling us our only purpose is pave the way for them?

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:17.560
Then why does the Colseit Branch even exist?

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:23.550
Logy-senpai, I found this on the ground just now.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:24.690
That's Escha's...

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.460
Escha?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.290
Escha!

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:36.750
Oh?

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.250
It's rare to see it raining.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.750
Hey, Escha-chan!

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.720
Take refuge from the rain here.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.420
What's wrong?

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:00.100
Duke-san, have you seen Escha?!

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.600
Yeah, she walked that way just now.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.100
Thanks!

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.490
Have you seen Escha?

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.160
If you're looking for Escha-san...

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.920
If I remember correctly, Escha-chan just went...

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.050
Escha!

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:40.970
Why are you out here?

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.480
I just wanted to see the view here.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:51.440
It's too bad, though.

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.570
Escha...

00:09:59.190 --> 00:09:59.910
Escha!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:05.370
It looks like there's nothing to see today...

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.510
Escha.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.650
Escha!

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:27.480
Ever since her mother, Miria, passed away, Escha would often gaze at those ruins.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:31.310
Why is she so interested in the Unexplored Ruins?

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.440
Did she hear a voice or something?

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.650
My oh my, I don't think that's the case.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:43.370
Escha has always said that somebody must live there.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.990
When she was still a child,

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:52.670
perhaps she thought the Unexplored Ruins was the kind of place her mother would be.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:57.800
Of course she wouldn't believe that now.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:02.790
But still, Escha still dreams of reaching the ruins from the bottom of her heart.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:06.510
Yeah, every time Escha gazes at the Unexplored Ruins,

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.930
her eyes shine very bright, just like a kid's.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.650
You're right.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:14.440
People who chase after their dreams always shine brightly.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:24.450
Ever since I was a kid, it's been my dream to go to those ruins.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:31.710
When she said that, I felt I could understand Escha for the first time.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.750
Marion-san!

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.090
Okay, so it's you this time?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.050
This time?

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.440
It's about this, isn't it?

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.310
The request for surveying the unexplored ruins from Threia.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.460
Yes!

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:52.810
We should accept the request, and survey the Unexplored Ruins first!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.520
No can do.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.480
Why?

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.440
Explain it to him.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:04.490
Central City ordered us to hold off on surveying the ruins until the team arrives.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:08.840
Which means we cannot accept the request for surveying the Unexplored Ruins.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.860
No way...

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:12.160
Wait... all of you too?

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.530
Yes.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.630
I thought it would cheer Escha up.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.670
I was thinking it would be a good idea.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.610
Even Wilbell and Nio-chan came by a moment ago, babbling excuses to me.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.210
"It's my fault that Escha-chan came down with a fever."

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.760
"Let's try to do something for her dream."

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.770
Geez, do you guys really think I'm okay with all this?

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:31.730
It's done!

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.510
Oh.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.510
So, what is it?

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:37.270
It's a request for permission to engage in certain activities.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:45.030
To help Central's survey team, the R&D Division will protect the ruins and secure a method to reach the ruins.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:48.120
Isn't that exactly what Central ordered us to do?

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.660
They're just having us pave the way for them.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:52.510
That's what it looks like on the surface,

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:58.170
but the details have far more in them than it appears at first glance.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.670
Could it be that, in order to find a way to reach the ruins...

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:09.260
It means that as we're responsible for developing a method to reach the ruins, we can try reaching them first?

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.310
Exactly!

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.270
Also, to protect the ruins...

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:20.150
We need to enter the ruins, and analyse what needs to be protected.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.070
Yes!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.460
I see!

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:30.950
This way Colseit Branch can begin its own survey before the people from Central arrive!

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.330
We can do our own thing while following Central City's instructions!

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:37.830
The two of you were both from Central until not long ago.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:42.050
T-That's true, but...

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.550
That's okay.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.510
I used to want to work in Central.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:52.260
Well, that was a long time ago, and I don't regret it one bit.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:54.980
Marion...

00:13:56.570 --> 00:14:01.760
R&D will start investigating the Unexplored
Ruins before Central City does.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:02.690
Yes!

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:09.570
Huh?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.740
Escha-san, you're rather late today.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.990
Yeah, I had a slight fever.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:16.200
Get better soon.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.540
Sorry I'm late!

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.160
Aren't you taking the day off?

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.830
Yes, but my fever broke.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.130
I see.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.690
The Branch Manager is out for breakfast,

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:32.630
so I'll record you showed up today.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:34.520
Thank you!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.770
Nobody is at R&D right now.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:46.280
The biggest problem with our plan is the branch manager.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:47.530
The branch manager is?

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:52.830
He used to be quite an active monster hunter in the Combat Department.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.830
Is he my senior?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.540
Even though I want to submit the request I just wrote,

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:58.910
it's impossible to deceive someone who understands the situation,

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.580
let alone someone who knows how to read these requests.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:06.350
He'll definitely figure out what our goal is.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:09.590
Does that mean our plan isn't going to work?

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.010
That's right.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:17.250
The branch manager didn't budge regardless of how Chief Marion complained about it.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.810
Marion, that's too bad.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:27.250
We won't know if we don't try!

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:28.360
Logy-kun?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.820
Branch Manager, I have something to ask of you.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.410
What is it, Logy-kun?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.370
Please accept this document.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.990
Here, of all places?

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:40.580
Yes.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:49.700
Fine.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.010
Is this a mission request?

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:04.710
I see.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.780
This is well written.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.790
Marion-kun, did you write this?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:09.860
Y-Yes!

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.890
I believe Central City will approve this.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:17.370
Solle will complain about the expenses, but he should have no problem with it as long as I persuade him.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.120
Then...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.400
No.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:24.430
Even if we could enter and survey the ruins through this request,

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.560
once the team from Central City arrives, everything shall be exposed.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.800
Even so...

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:36.980
Even so, we want to let Escha investigate the ruins herself!

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:37.590
We want to make her dreams-

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:39.810
And after that?

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:43.440
In the worst case scenario, it will destroy the Colseit Branch.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.190
It looks like you understand.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:52.240
I will ask Central City to allow us to participate in their survey.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.250
Understand?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.600
It's fine if a rubbish branch like yours is destroyed.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:57.200
What?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.820
Duke?

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:00.450
Duke-san?

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:05.670
Yo, Chief, tell me why the Colseit Branch was set up again.

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:09.990
Obviously it was to survey the Unexplored Ruins.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.950
Ain't it?

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:15.340
Isn't surveying the Unexplored Ruins the entire branch's dream?

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:20.070
If you can't even do that, then what's the point of keeping the branch going?

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:24.270
H-However, it's also the branch's responsibility to protect the wellbeing of the town...

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.230
Protect our wellbeing?

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:30.560
What's so funny?

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:35.430
Isn't it? You? Protecting our wellbeing?

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:37.070
Stop acting all high and mighty.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:43.150
Haven't we always been chasing after our dreams?!

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:43.870
What are you talking about?

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.500
Have you forgotten?

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:53.630
When we were still in Combat, we would always beer up and talk about our dreams every time we beat a monster!

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.970
We would tell each other how we wanted to visit the Unexplored Ruins,

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:59.140
and that we would go wild if there were monsters there!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:03.560
We always talked about what would be waiting for us, and what weapons would be effective against them!

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.020
Didn't we?!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.940
We were even butt naked until the morning.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.200
What? Naked?

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:13.980
Branch Manager...

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.170
You misunderstood him!

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.750
We weren't naked!

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.450
It was this guy who kept forcing ale on me!

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.870
You would even take bitches home every night while you were hammered.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:29.040
Shut it, Duke!

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.500
Your muscles' been deteriorating!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.810
I'm still on the job!

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.380
Aren't you the one who bailed on us first?!

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.180
You've been rotting away behind a desk, haven't you?!

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:45.950
I can say the same.

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:47.600
Your kneecap's crying for help!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:55.090
C-Chief, the pub's being wrecked!

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:57.240
Linca, stop them!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.020
I don't think I can.

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:01.780
Awin-kun! Logy-kun!

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:03.870
No way.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.450
That's almost like a battle between monsters.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:12.290
Even if you're made of muscle, going for the stomach always work!

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:15.090
Hell, even your brain's rotting!

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:22.510
Stop it!

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:30.630
Duke-san? Branch Manager?!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:40.780
Escha!

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.610
Escha-chan!

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:56.320
Hey, how long has it been since we last went so far?

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:57.140
Are you okay, Escha?

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.670
Geez, you haven't changed.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.180
You haven't either, Chief.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.310
I see.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.890
Nothing has changed.

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:12.640
In that case, we can just join another branch's combat squad even if ours is destroyed.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:13.930
That's right.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.520
If you're up for it, I'll follow you any time.

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:23.780
I'll submit this request to Central City, Marion-kun.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.160
Branch Manager, you mean...?!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.330
Yes, I approve it.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.040
Be it the Unexplored Ruins or anywhere else, it's best to follow your heart.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:36.000
You are free to investigate anywhere you want.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:39.630
No matter what happens, I will accept all responsibility.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:42.840
Huh?

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.010
The Unexplored... Ruins?

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.710
That's right, Escha!

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:49.230
We can go to the Unexplored Ruins!

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.270
The Branch Manager gave us permission!

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:54.020
It's fine already, Escha!

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.830
This is Chief Marion's idea!

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.470
That's not all!

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:02.190
Logy-kun was the one who first suggested it to the branch manager!

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:06.160
No... I... well...

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:07.780
Logy-san...

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:12.660
No, I...

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:18.630
Thanks, everyone!

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:55.180
I can hear her.

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:57.650
What did she say?

00:22:57.650 --> 00:22:59.890
"I... don't need humans."

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:00.440
Huh?

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.970
"This world doesn't need humans,"

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:07.740
is what she said?

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.490
They are impatient,

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:12.750
they betray,

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:14.210
they lie,

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:16.150
they don't do what they said they would,

00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:17.590
they can't make up their mind,

00:23:17.590 --> 00:23:19.390
they don't work together,

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:21.210
and they don't try hard enough.

00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:24.750
Humans are too soft.

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:26.020
And that's why...

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:27.810
...we don't need humans.
